WEBVTT

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:04.380
<i>Behold, the vast world in which we live!</i>

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.740
<i>It is rampant with monsters 
that threaten human life.</i>

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:16.310
<i>This threat is opposed by 
countless adventurers! Heroes!</i>

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.470
<i>Every day, they face these 
dangerous battles...</i>

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.580
<i>To protect the people! To protect the world!</i>

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.290
And I, Alvin, am one of them!

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.510
<i>Now in a party with Carla, the healer,</i>

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.700
<i>my journey continues!</i>

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.370
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.370
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.370
My Healer!

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:15.150
<b>"Forced to travel with Carla, a healer..."</b>

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.530
I'm pretty sure this is the right way...

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:29.160
Where exactly are we going, 
and what are we doing, Alvin-san?

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.490
We're gathering antidote herbs.

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:33.850
It's a quest I received from 
the Adventurers Guild.

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:39.160
My fight with the Mostly Bear kept me 
from reaching my destination yesterday.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.700
Gathering antidote herbs?

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.970
That's a quest for beginners, isn't it?

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:56.220
That should be just the right level of difficulty 
for a rookie adventurer like you, Alvin-san.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.060
Aren't you a healer?

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.020
Shouldn't the things you say 
make people feel <i>better</i>?

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:01.810
<i>Freaking hell.</i>

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:05.970
<i>If not for that stupid curse, 
I'd have ditched her ages ago!</i>

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:06.910
Alvin-san.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:10.050
Are you certain that this is the right way?

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.350
Yeah, it should be right down this road.

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:17.920
Does that mean we'll have 
to pass through there?

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.370
Alvin-san, to your right!

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.900
Now, to the north-northwest!

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.170
Not that way! 
Twenty degrees right diagonal!

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.310
Now! At eight o'clock 
plus fifty-two minutes!

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.130
Next, the ox-tiger direction!

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.180
What's wrong? 
Are you hard of hearing?

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.590
Hey!

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:17.590
Your instructions are impossible to f—

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.190
Are you having a picnic?!

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.900
What's <i>wrong</i> with you?

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.680
How can you be drinking 
tea while I'm fighting?

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:30.940
Say something!

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:32.350
I'm just taking a little break.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:35.160
You've got a whole brunch setup on here!

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.260
You don't have to be so mad...

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:39.870
I made enough sandwiches 
for you, too, Alvin-san.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.910
That's not what I'm mad about!

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:42.920
And I ate them!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.940
Now <i>that</i> I'm mad about!

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.520
We can't move on until we 
beat these guys, remember?

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.540
Feels a little chilly today, huh?

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.680
Must be a ghost thing, huh?

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.070
But I'm stuck here fighting all on my own...

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.610
Couldn't you help me out a little?

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:05.360
What's with that expression?

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.630
You're aware that physical attacks 
don't work on ghosts, right?

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.420
You need silver weapons or magic.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:16.760
Is that true?

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.570
Oh, I'm so sorry!

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:22.860
Hey, where's this coming from?!

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:26.580
I knew you were a beginner, and yet...

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.240
If only I'd told you that in advance,

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.960
you wouldn't have been forced to 
humiliate yourself like this!

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:32.870
How embarrassing.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.980
I... I didn't humiliate myself!

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.740
Everyone makes a mistake 
or two in their life!

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.970
And besides, this is my 
first time fighting ghosts!

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.990
Hey, calm down already.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.500
Calm down?! You little...

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:49.340
That way you were dancing...

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:55.400
I mean, the way you were fighting 
earlier looked really cool!

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.500
With moves like that, 
you could get into the circus!

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.080
What am I, a clown to you?!

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.940
You should take it as a compliment!

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:05.140
They make laughingstocks out of themselves 
just to give other people a good time!

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.590
I wasn't trying to give 
other people a good time!

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.290
Sheesh. Like she knows so 
much about everything...

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:13.350
If you're going to lecture me, 
you could at least try to contribute!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.870
Excuse me? Have you forgotten my class?

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.090
Stress-maker?

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.400
Harrumph!

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.860
At least call me a stress goddess!

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.640
You see what I mean?

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:28.280
It's quite obvious that I am a healer.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.700
In other words, a holy woman!

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:30.420
Big doubts there!

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:33.820
I exist to bring comfort to lost souls.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:36.570
What? So you'll unleash a 
light spell or something?

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:41.080
Hopeless child. So quick to 
solve everything with violence!

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.620
It's so sad!

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.620
"Sad" certainly describes how I'm feeling...

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:46.020
Sad!

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.350
Seriously, drop it.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:52.640
Ghosts are fated to wander this 
world due to unfinished business.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:56.850
All we need to do is resolve 
whatever's bothering them.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.000
I see!

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.530
And you think you can do that?

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.890
I think if I just hear out their stories,

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:08.200
and say things like "poor thing!" and 
"that's pretty rough!" they'll pass on.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:09.520
Easy-peasy.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:10.890
What is this, a girls' night out?

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.400
We'll start with you.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:13.790
What, me?

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.160
Do you have any regrets in life?

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.270
Y-Yes...

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.210
I was twenty years old when I died.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:25.410
It happened just two weeks after 
getting my first girlfriend!

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.220
Poor thing! That's pretty rough!

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:29.630
Super-bad times!

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:32.550
Don't mock the dead, you holy fraud!

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.170
And did you actually say "super-bad times"?

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.220
Incidentally, Alvin-san is thirty years old,

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.650
and he says he's never dated a woman.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.640
She mocks the living, too.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.970
Thank you. I guess I was a lucky man!

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.850
And now the dead are mocking me.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:51.890
Excuse me.

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:52.480
Yes?

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.210
I used to be a warrior.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:58.120
But I was killed by a golem! 
It's so frustrating!

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.510
Alvin-san, can you defeat a golem?

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:05.700
Well, I was hoping to face 
one sooner or later.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:08.660
But right now, five slimes 
is about the best I can do.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.220
Five slimes?!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:17.890
Scrub! I'm ded! Trollolol!

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:17.890
I thought so!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.820
Incredible!

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.140
We're sending them all to their final rest!

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:23.820
And laughing as they go!

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:25.290
He was laughing <i>at me</i>!

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.770
You might have a future in this, Alvin-san!

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.230
A future? What kind?

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:33.980
It takes an exceptional person 
to help a ghost rest in peace!

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:36.170
I think you really have what it takes!

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:38.030
Are you light-element affiliated?

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.050
O Warrior of Light!

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.520
O Holy Knight!

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.030
Hey, lay off...

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:44.040
O Circus Performer?

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.000
I'm not a clown!

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:53.310
Well, we made it through the graveyard,

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:54.210
but now I'm exhausted.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:09:01.100
We could have stayed there longer and helped 
all the ghosts find their final rest.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:06.100
Alvin, Warrior of Light, 
offers free passage
to the next life!!

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.100
Don't be stupid!

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.090
I'm a warrior, start to finish!

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:11.150
I'm not about to change classes!

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:14.750
I feel like it's a waste of your 
talent, but if you insist.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:19.340
It's a common saying: "A person's ambitions 
don't always match their talents."

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:22.240
Imagine I said the exact same thing to you.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.110
Now, let's go.

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:26.440
We still haven't finished our quest!

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:31.990
Alvin-san?

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.030
Alvin-san?

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:40.010
People tend to think of gathering 
antidote herbs as an easy quest,

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:41.880
but there are many things 
you need to watch out for.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:46.040
This forest, in particular, 
is rife with goblins!

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.940
They're not strong, but they're tricky!

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:54.510
If you're not careful, 
you'll end up in a goblin trap!

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.800
Like I just did.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:13.410
Are you all right?!

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:16.300
Is that how you check on someone?

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:19.480
Thank goodness! I was so worried!

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:21.420
You seem pretty relaxed to me!

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:23.170
How are you feeling?

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:25.300
I'm feel extremely ashamed.

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:28.910
One of those, "I'd like to crawl into a 
hole and never come out" feelings, right?

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:33.830
Well, I guess you succeeded there!

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:35.430
Could you please be quiet?

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:37.170
Can you get out?

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:38.580
I'll try.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.290
This won't be easy.

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.580
The ground breaks apart too easily.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:47.320
There wouldn't happen to be something 
like a rope around, would there?

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.110
Something like a rope?

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.310
You mean like intestines?

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:51.970
That idea is insane!

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:55.300
Not even a necromancer would 
come up with "intestines"

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.470
when asked for something like a rope!

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:01.110
But you can't expect a rope 
to just fall into my lap.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:03.470
And you think intestines would?!

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.740
A vine from the trees would be just as good!

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.160
Could you please just hurry?

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.940
If a monster shows up now, 
I'm a sitting duck!

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.220
Very well!

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:13.950
I'll go searching.

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.500
Hey! Don't go too far!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:19.870
Remember, I'll die if we 
get 300 meters apart!

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.430
Were you waiting long?

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:24.380
Not long at all, actually!

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.600
That exchange just now...

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:29.720
It sounded like a couple 
meeting up for a date.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:30.690
Unpleasant.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:31.860
What in the world...

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.830
And did you even look?

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:35.890
I'm sorry.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.890
I didn't see anything that 
looked like intestines.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:40.000
That sounds like a good thing.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.140
But I did run into a person, 
so I called them here.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:44.770
Right over here!

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:47.130
A person? In this forest?

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:49.890
He's the one who dug the hole!

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.730
That's a freaking goblin!

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.340
What, is that bad?

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:54.540
Yes, it's very bad!

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.530
Why did you call a monster here?!

00:11:56.530 --> 00:12:00.470
Are you really in a position 
to be choosy right now?

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:01.520
You bet your ass I am!

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:04.080
When he looks at me, he sees—

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:04.790
Wait...

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:08.140
Why's he crying?

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:11.260
What's wrong, Gobkichi-san?

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:12.970
You're already introduced?

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:14.790
Why are you crying?

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.360
I think Alvin-san is the one 
who should be crying!

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:18.910
I mean, look at the situation he's in!

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:20.420
No kidding!

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:27.010
I dug that hole to catch wild boars...

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:28.190
Gobkichi-san...

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.890
And now... this...

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.360
I'm so pathetic!

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:35.070
Apologize!

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:36.310
Me?!

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:53.070
We're almost at the place where 
the antidote herbs grow, right?

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:54.860
Hush!

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:56.340
This isn't good...

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:57.960
It's a cyclops!

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:00.670
We've got to get out of 
here before he sees us!

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:02.390
Wait a minute!

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:04.230
Are you sure that's what you want to do?

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:09.740
A person can't mature if they avoid 
anything that might challenge them.

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:11.780
Over time, such people...

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.560
turn out just like you, Alvin-san!

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.320
I'm already like me!

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:18.960
That's why we should beat him ourselves!

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:19.990
Yeah!

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:21.690
Don't say "yeah!"

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.560
I just said that five slimes was my limit!

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.910
So... do you have a plan 
to beat him or something?

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:33.280
I have the ultimate, secret plan known as me!

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:34.040
Isn't that nice?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.070
Please keep it a secret forever!

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:38.580
So, what were you intending to do?

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.110
Tut, tut!

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:43.550
Alvin-san. Remember, I'm a healer!

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.470
<b>Ta-da</b>

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.460
So I'll use summoning magic!

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:48.370
Do healers do that?

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:52.740
All the hip, young healers 
are into summoning magic!

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:55.110
I wish they were into common sense!

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:58.090
So? What exactly do you intend to summon?

00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:00.650
Would you like to see what they look like?

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:05.370
For the lowest level summoned beast, 
I don't even need a ritual.

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.760
For real? Sure, show me!

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:09.160
I kind of want to see it!

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:10.380
Very well.

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:16.580
Put it back!

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:19.300
What are you?! A servant of the devil?!

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:20.620
What do you expect?

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:22.380
It's the lowest level kind, after all.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.230
With a proper ritual,

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:28.600
I can call a proper summoned beast.

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.640
Although it will take some time...

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:33.180
Now that you mention it,

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.040
shouldn't you start summoning right now,

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.520
before the Cyclops notices us?

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.160
I can't do that. No way!

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:41.300
Why not?!

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:44.130
It doesn't feel dramatic enough.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:46.290
It doesn't need to be entertaining!

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:49.970
By the way, you've been making a 
lot of noise for a while now...

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:52.350
Why do you think that is?!

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:54.280
...so he's already noticed us.

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:06.180
We're... We're not actually ready.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:08.150
Oh, okay. I'll wait.

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:09.820
Why's he so damn nice?!

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:11.380
He said he'll wait!

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.060
No need for that.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:15.420
I've already prepared for the summoning.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:16.550
What is that?!

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:19.090
I'll launch this into the air...

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:22.300
and it will travel through dimensions, 
and reach the summoned beast!

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.890
Then the summoned beast will 
come running to our aid!

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:27.820
It's my brilliantly unique summoning method!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.820
Go!

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:39.330
Hey, it's coming back.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:45.110
It's from my summoned beast.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.710
"I've been asked to babysit 
the neighborhood kids,

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.910
so I can't come."

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:50.460
How very considerate!

00:15:50.690 --> 00:15:51.620
So?

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:54.460
You need something from these rocks?

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.930
Well... actually... that is...

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:03.290
So, you're trying to gather antidote herbs?

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:06.100
You could've just said so earlier!

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:08.850
Well, thanks for showing us the way...

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:12.250
Well, these rocks are my turf,

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:15.270
so I know the way better than you.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:17.870
And the antidote herbs are this way?

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.350
Yeah, they're right here.

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.240
Take as many as you like!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:30.720
Use them to help someone suffering 
the ravages of poison!

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:31.450
Later!

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.870
Thanks again!

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:35.570
Thank you so much!

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.790
What a nice guy!

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.350
I'm glad I didn't call that summoned beast.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:43.520
My intuition was right on the money!

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:44.980
You just got lucky!

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:48.320
And I'm feeling pretty good right now, 
so could you please not ruin it?

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:58.410
I'm glad we got lots of herbs, 
but the sun's down already...

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.250
We'll have to camp out tonight.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:01.510
I suppose...

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:03.990
Boy, I'm exhausted.

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:05.770
I'm as exhausted as a man can be!

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:09.020
<i>Since forming a party with Carla,</i>

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:11.680
<i>I've felt forms of exhaustion 
I never knew before.</i>

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:15.760
<i>Being in a party is way 
harder than I expected.</i>

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:19.190
<i>I figured partying up with a healer 
would make everything easier...</i>

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:24.430
<i>That said... is she even really a healer?</i>

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:27.240
<i>She pulled out that creepy 
summoned beast earlier today...</i>

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.610
<i>Does she even know any proper spells?</i>

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:33.280
<i>I don't think Mostly Bear-san would lie,</i>

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:36.410
<i>so I assume she really did heal me,</i>

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:38.890
<i>but she was also wearing 
that weird outfit...</i>

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:42.370
<i>Maybe the reason I'm really 
getting so tired so often</i>

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:46.060
<i>is because she's an evil witch 
draining my life force?</i>

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:49.030
<i>Maybe, while I still can...</i>

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:49.890
<i>No, no!</i>

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:52.870
<i>Remember, you'll die if you 
get 300 meters away from her!</i>

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:54.880
<i>I can't even run away!</i>

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:59.010
<i>Well, it's true that other than the curse 
and the mental stress she's caused,</i>

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:01.410
<i>she hasn't done me any harm...</i>

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:03.650
<i>I guess I should just wait 
and see a little longer.</i>

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:08.470
<i>Look at her, not even caring how I feel!</i>

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:12.140
What's with all the fidgeting, anyway?

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:16.910
Well... at times like these... you know...

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:19.410
We're supposed to talk 
about who we like, right?!

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:21.700
It's not a dang sleepover!

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:23.150
What, it isn't?!

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:25.110
Camping isn't some game!

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:27.670
Dangerous monsters come out at night!

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:29.540
We have to take turns standing watch,

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:32.070
keep our wits about us, and...

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.410
What are you laughing about?

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.070
Oh... I'm sorry.

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:39.840
I just found it extremely funny 
to receive a high-handed lecture

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:42.680
from a person so green 
that he fell into a hole.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:45.430
I really wish you could 
work on that phrasing!

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:48.200
Still, you're acting a little goofy now.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:49.980
Are you enjoying yourself?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.700
I wouldn't say that.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.600
But this is my first time camping out.

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:00.980
So I suppose it feels rather 
like a new experience,

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:03.590
and I feel kind of like a real adventurer...

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:06.780
And I guess it is fun.

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:09.570
What about you, Alvin-san?

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:14.080
I've camped out several times.

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:20.590
But I guess it is... my first time 
doing it with a real companion.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.370
Alvin-san...

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:25.270
You don't have any friends?

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:26.590
You don't, either!

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:29.470
Here we go.

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:30.600
Time for bed.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:31.950
It seems a bit early for that.

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:33.440
Are you an old man?

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.250
It's talking with you that 
makes me feel tired!

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:41.470
You seem pretty wide awake, 
so I'll rest first.

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:43.100
I don't mind, of course.

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:46.970
Falling into that hole must have 
been very mentally taxing.

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:49.370
The only thing taxing here is you!

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:54.120
Anyway, wake me up in three hours.

00:19:54.490 --> 00:19:55.670
Understood.

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.620
In the meantime, I'll...

00:19:57.620 --> 00:19:59.340
Stand watch, right?

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:00.770
...sing a song.

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:01.760
Why?

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:05.010
What a strange question!

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:07.940
If you wanna talk "strange," let's 
talk about how your mind works!

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:09.500
Did your brain short out or something?!

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:11.720
Well, I was going to sing a lullaby.

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:13.240
Here I go...

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:15.660
Despite what you might think, 
I really do love singing.

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:17.770
I wish you'd love <i>silence</i>.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:22.930
And they say my singing voice 
draws birds out of the skies!

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:25.150
With what, the shock waves?

00:20:25.150 --> 00:20:26.940
And you still suck at winking.

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:29.650
Please, just trust me and listen!

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:32.400
Well... I might as well give you a chance.

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:40.780
Neeryooom! Chugga-chugga-chugga-chug!

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.170
Okay, stop!

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:43.170
But that was just the intro!

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:45.530
What kind of lullaby has an intro?!

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:48.420
And what kind of lullaby goes that hard?!

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:51.550
I'll try a more peaceful one, then.

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:53.170
That should've been your first go-to!

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.520
I'll begin, then.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:21:00.300
<i>Go to sleep... Go to sleep...</i>

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:08.780
<i>Listen to my calming song... and sleep...</i>

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:09.670
She's not bad.

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:13.580
<i>Then fall into the abyss of endless fear,</i>

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:17.680
<i>be tormented by nightmares, never waking,</i>

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:19.780
<i>as you writhe in agony...</i>

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:20.830
Is this a curse?!

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:21.810
How rude!

00:21:21.810 --> 00:21:23.990
That song was guaranteed 
to put you in a slumber!

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:25.330
An <i>eternal</i> slumber, maybe!

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:27.000
I've been wondering since we met,

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:29.070
but are you really even a healer?!

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.270
Crap! I yelled too loud 
and summoned a monster!

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.440
Could you people shut up?!

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.410
Don't you know what time it is?!

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:44.940
He's yelling at us!

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:47.030
Get to sleep already!

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:48.740
Yes, sir!

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:27.310
Next episode's title is

00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:32.390
"Despite the terrible time he's been having 
during his travels with Carla the healer

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:37.240
for two episodes Alvin tries to keep up 
his job as a monster-hunting adventurer

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:40.050
<b>"Despite the terrible time he's been having during his travels with Carla
the healer for two episodes Alvin tries to keep up his job as a
monster-hunting adventurer which I guess shows some pretty impressive
resolve except when he runs into a mushroom monster he challenges
to a fight and it turns out to be tougher than expected and by the way 
this won't get mentioned in the series proper but his species is called 
matango and you might think it has an adult male voice but also 
given how it was drawn in the manga a childish voice might
work too, and it's just one big surprise after another, but the truth is
we actually wrote this title in early 2021 before we cast the voice actor,
so I'm actually looking forward to who's voicing it but anyway there's
more going on than the question of whether Alvin can beat the
mushroom and that's the deal with episode 3."</b>

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:40.100
which I guess shows some 
pretty impressive resolve..."
